g vaccinated the question is will  those antibodies still stick to this  version of the spike protein or will it  evade that protection we need to find  that out to be honest though that's  going to take two three weeks in both  laboratory and field studies to figure  out the answer and that's what all of us  as scientists want to know  and very quickly because i know you say  you don't really know much about this  variant but when you have these doctors  in the south african medical association  including one who actually spotted this  variant  down in south africa and he says you  know the symptoms tend to be mild is it  too early to make that declaration  i think it's too early trace i think the  initial cases were mostly young people  who tend to have mild infections anyway  we need more data there before we could  say confidently that this is not a  severe version of the virus but we  should find that out in the next couple  of weeks so dr collins let's move on now  the president has put a travel ban in  eight south african countries let's put  those on the screen here's the  vaccination rates of those countries you  can see they go all the way up to 27 in  lesotho and then all the way down to 3.2  percent in malawi which is  extraordinarily low the former biden  advisor dr zeke emanuel said the  following and i'm quoting here  restricting travel is going to slow it's  coming not stop it from coming the fact  that it's coming here is inevitable the  environment in which it comes may not be  inevitable we can alter the environment  and if it's just a case of trying to  slow it down dr collins why not put in  place more travel bans because the  people in south africa some of the  government officials there feel like  they're being singled out feel like this  is a little bit discriminatory against  them  well i think it is a difficult decision  trace and this is just the best advice  of the public health experts and you'll  notice other countries like the uk and  